@startuml j6-clinic-file-edit
!include style.iuml
title J6 Edit the clinic file on /staff
actor Staff
participant "Staff page\n(staff/index.html, staff.js)" as SP
participant "core.js" as Core
database "localStorage" as LS
participant "Chat page\n(index.html, chat.js)" as Chat
actor Patient
autonumber

Staff -> SP : opens /staff
SP -> Core : FD.loadClinic(), then clinicEditor()
Core -> LS : read frontdesk.clinic (else the shipped clinic-data.json)
SP --> Staff : #clinic-json filled with the file in use, #clinic-name set
opt v1.1: Staff use "Edit with a form" (#clinic-form, closed by default)
  Staff -> SP : opens "Edit with a form"
  SP -> SP : form.js builds the fields (ids cf-...) from the JSON in #clinic-json
  note right of SP
  v1.1. The fields follow the file's own shape, so a file
  in another shape gets a form too. An "Assistant" section
  holds the optional name (at most 40 characters) and the
  quick replies (at most 8: label at most 24, question at
  most 120 characters).
  end note
  Staff -> SP : changes a field
  SP -> SP : the form writes the change into the same #clinic-json box
  note right of SP : nothing is written unless a field was changed; the same "Save clinic file" button stores it
end
Staff -> SP : edits the JSON (or used the form, v1.1), presses #clinic-save ("Save clinic file")
SP -> SP : JSON.parse()
alt not valid JSON
  SP --> Staff : "This is not valid JSON: <parser message>"
else parsed
  SP -> Core : FD.validateClinic(obj)
  alt a check fails
    Core --> SP : message
    note right of Core
    Must be an object with a "clinic" section (name, phone,
    emergency_phone, whatsapp, address as text) and an "hours"
    section with at least one text entry; "services" and
    "doctors", when present, must be lists.
    end note
    SP --> Staff : the message
  else valid
    SP -> Core : FD.saveClinic(obj)
    Core -> LS : write frontdesk.clinic
    SP -> SP : clinicEditor()
    SP --> Staff : "Saved. The chat now answers from this file."
    LS -> Chat : storage event, key frontdesk.clinic (another tab)
    Chat -> Core : FD.clinic()
    Chat -> Chat : data = the edited file; side(), labels()
    Patient -> Chat : asks a question
    Chat -> Core : FD.answer(q, data)
    note right of Chat : the answer, the guard and the file sent to api/chat all use the edited file
    Chat --> Patient : reply from the edited file
  end
end
opt Staff presses #clinic-reset
  SP -> Core : FD.resetClinic()
  Core -> LS : remove frontdesk.clinic
  SP --> Staff : "Back to the original clinic file."
  LS -> Chat : storage event, key frontdesk.clinic
  Chat -> Core : FD.clinic() returns the shipped file
end
participant "Shared store\n(api/clinic.js, api/_store.js,\nPostgres clinic_data)" as Store
group v1.4: the file for every device (shared.js)
  SP -> Store : POST /api/clinic { clinic } or { reset: true }, x-desk-code
  Store --> SP : saved for every device, or the part that failed
  Patient -> Chat : asks the next question, on any device
  Chat -> Store : GET /api/clinic (2 s at most; an emergency never waits)
  Store --> Chat : the saved file
  Chat -> Core : FD.saveClinic, then the answer from the saved file
end
@enduml
